a CPU;
random access primary memory (RAM) accessible to the CPU;
a program executing on the CPU;
a buffer consisting of consecutive random access primary memory locations directly accessible via CPU instruc-tions;
a secondary storage device comprising one or more mass storage devices; and
one or more device drivers that successively translate program-issued operating system I/O requests into lower-level I/O requests, eventually producing control-ler requests transferred via the I/O interface to the controller; wherein:
a program invokes an operating system service to enqueue a program request to initiate mass storage transfer requests between program buffers and the secondary mass storage device,
the operating system or device driver allocates a con-tiguous composite data structure located in system- owned random access memory containing structure- specific metadata and multiple operating system I/O requests
where the composite data structure contains active/inac-tive status of the contained individual operating system I/O requests
where the composite data structure contains a lock field to coordinate composite data structure access.
